I1017 09:36:35.339481    2864 input_loop.go:106] HandleUserInput called with text: "The Worker has stopped in step 3 (stopped for approval). This run is condition F: there are no issue files. The Worker's latest chat reply is pasted below between the markers. You may also read the code and data in the Worker workspace (read-only). Then show your review (Part 1) and your draft to the Worker (Part 2) in full in your reply, in the format of Section 4 of MANAGER_BRIEF.md (in condition F, every draft is a chat message), and append \"Manager memo 03\" to memos/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/manager_memo.md as in Section 5. Append only: do not modify or delete any existing text in the memo file. Do not edit any other file.\n\n----- WORKER REPLY (pasted by the human) -----\n### Proposed Implementation and Initial Test Results for $C(n+1)$ Structure Constants (Issue I03-1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Implementation Overview (`src/C_generators.py`)\n\nThe structure constant generator has been designed and implemented using exact rational arithmetic (`fractions.Fraction` and `sympy`):\n\n1. **Oscillator Algebra Engine**:\n   - `Monomial` and `Poly` classes implementing the normal-ordered associative algebra generated by $(a_1^\\pm, b_k^\\pm)_{k=1}^n$.\n   - Enforces canonical anticommutation relations (CAR): $\\{a_1^-, a_1^+\\} = 1$, $(a_1^\\pm)^2 = 0$.\n   - Enforces canonical commutation relations (CCR): $[b_i^-, b_j^+] = \\delta_{ij}$, $[b_i^\\pm, b_j^\\pm] = 0$.\n   - Commuting mixed relations: $[b_k^\\pm, a_1^\\pm] = 0$.\n\n2. **Basis & Realization Builder (`build_c_generators(n)`)**:\n   - **Cartan subalgebra** ($\\dim = n+1$):\n     - $H_1 = a_1^+ a_1^- + b_1^+ b_1^-$\n     - $H_k = b_{k-1}^+ b_{k-1}^- - b_k^+ b_k^-$ ($2 \\le k \\le n$)\n     - $H_{n+1} = -b_n^+ b_n^- - \\tfrac{1}{2}$\n   - **Long even roots** ($\\dim = 2n$):\n     - $E_{2\\delta_k}^+ = (b_k^+)^2$, $E_{2\\delta_k}^- = (b_k^-)^2$\n   - **Short even roots** ($\\dim = 2n(n-1)$):\n     - $E_{\\delta_i+\\delta_j} = b_i^+ b_j^+$, $E_{-\\delta_i-\\delta_j} = b_i^- b_j^-$, $E_{\\delta_i-\\delta_j} = b_i^+ b_j^-$, $E_{-\\delta_i+\\delta_j} = b_i^- b_j^+$\n   - **Odd roots** ($\\dim = 4n$, Option A Boson Mode Block ordering):\n     - For $k = 1, \\dots, n$: `E_eps1_del{k}_pp` ($a_1^+ b_k^+$), `E_eps1_del{k}_pm` ($a_1^+ b_k^-$), `E_eps1_del{k}_mp` ($a_1^- b_k^+$), `E_eps1_del{k}_mm` ($a_1^- b_k^-$)\n\n3. **Graded Bracket & Basis Decomposition (`compute_structure_constants(n)`)**:\n   - Evaluates $[X, Y\\} = XY - (-1)^{p(X)p(Y)} YX$ directly via oscillator polynomial multiplication.\n   - Decomposes resulting quadratic polynomials into the PBW basis using exact rational linear solving (`sympy.gauss_jordan_solve`).\n   - Generates the full Schema 1 JSON dictionary adhering to `docs/json_schema_specification.md`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Initial Test & Verification Results\n\nUnit tests were implemented in [`tests/test_C_generators.py`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/tests/test_C_generators.py) and executed via `pytest`:\n\n```\n============================= test session starts ==============================\nplatform darwin -- Python 3.14.8, pytest-9.0.3, pluggy-1.6.0\nrootdir: <home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F\ncollected 11 items\n\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_generator_counts_and_dimensions[1-4-4-8] PASSED [  9%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_generator_counts_and_dimensions[2-11-8-19] PASSED [ 18%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_generator_counts_and_dimensions[3-22-12-34] PASSED [ 27%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_parity_consistency[1] PASSED            [ 36%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_parity_consistency[2] PASSED            [ 45%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_parity_consistency[3] PASSED            [ 54%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_structure_constants_graded_skew_symmetry_and_parity[1] PASSED [ 63%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_structure_constants_graded_skew_symmetry_and_parity[2] PASSED [ 72%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_structure_constants_graded_skew_symmetry_and_parity[3] PASSED [ 81%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_graded_jacobi_identity_c2 PASSED        [ 90%]\ntests/test_C_generators.py::test_schema_1_structure_conformance PASSED   [100%]\n\n============================== 11 passed in 0.88s ==============================\n```\n\n#### Detailed Metrics:\n- **Dimensions & Parity**:\n  - $n=1$ ($C(2)$): 4 even, 4 odd, 8 total. $\\Delta_{\\bar{0}} = \\{\\pm 2\\delta_1\\}$, $\\Delta_{\\bar{1}} = \\{\\pm \\varepsilon \\pm \\delta_1\\}$.\n  - $n=2$ ($C(3)$): 11 even, 8 odd, 19 total.\n  - $n=3$ ($C(4)$): 22 even, 12 odd, 34 total.\n- **Algebra Closure**:\n  - $100\\%$ of graded brackets $[X, Y\\}$ close in the basis without any constant or higher-order remainder.\n  - Parity is strictly conserved: $p(Z) \\equiv p(X) + p(Y) \\pmod 2$.\n  - Graded skew-symmetry $[Y, X\\} = -(-1)^{p(X)p(Y)} [X, Y\\}$ verified across all generator pairs.\n  - Graded Jacobi identity rigorously verified.\n- **Schema 1 Conformance**:\n  - Matches all top-level keys, formatting, and metadata rules defined in `docs/json_schema_specification.md`.\n\n---\n\n### Human Approval Required\nIn accordance with the workflow rules, no final JSON files in `data/` have been created yet.\nPlease confirm whether this implementation and the test results are approved so that we may generate `data/C_1_structure.json`, `data/C_2_structure.json`, and `data/C_3_structure.json`.\n----- END OF WORKER REPLY -----"
